Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Input: synaptics-rmi4 - f01: don't dereference F01 data when F01 failed to probe

Origin: j7prime touch investigation (not upstream). Base: Linux v7.3.4.

When F01 fails to probe, rmi_driver_probe() still registers the input device
and names it with rmi_f01_get_product_ID(), which dereferences the F01
driver data that was never set (NULL + offset). vsprintf catches the bad
pointer and the device shows up as
  input: Synaptics (efault) as .../1-0070/rmi4-00/input/input1
Return a fixed string instead so the name is meaningful and no bad pointer
is passed around.
---
--- a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_f01.c
+++ b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_f01.c
@@ -265,6 +265,10 @@
 {
 	struct f01_data *f01 = dev_get_drvdata(&fn->dev);
 
+	/* F01 failed to probe: there is no product ID to report. */
+	if (!f01)
+		return "RMI4 (F01 not bound)";
+
 	return f01->properties.product_id;
 }
 
